  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A microprocessor is attached to a metal heat sink to prevent overheating. The diagram below shows two interfaces where thermal energy is transferred.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Which row correctly identifies the primary mechanisms of thermal energy transfer at interface <strong>1</strong> and interface <strong>2</strong>?</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Interface 1</th><th>Interface 2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-label=\"A\"><td><strong>A</strong></td><td>Conduction</td><td>Convection</td></tr><tr data-label=\"B\"><td><strong>B</strong></td><td>Conduction</td><td>Radiation</td></tr><tr data-label=\"C\"><td><strong>C</strong></td><td>Convection</td><td>Conduction</td></tr><tr data-label=\"D\"><td><strong>D</strong></td><td>Radiation</td><td>Convection</td></tr></tbody></table>"
  },
